From e92f9f1aa343c2b668d40797fa50137fde9afaf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MidAutumnMoon <me@418.im>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:37:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] highlight: add fish_color_symlink

Mark argument tokens whose final path component is a symlink (dangling
ones included) with a new HighlightSpec::symlink bit, resolved through
the fish_color_symlink variable after the valid_path merge so a set
variable wins on symlink characters. Unset applies the built-in default
"magenta --underline=dashed" (zero config); an empty value parses to a
no-op face and restores stock rendering.

is_potential_path returns PathTest { is_path, is_symlink } with
lstat/d_type semantics only, so the signal never follows the link and is
cursor-stable. is_path semantics are unchanged. cd paths and redirection
targets are out of scope.

Fork patch; no shell upstream highlights symlinks on the command line.
See FISH-FORK markers at each hunk.
